WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.310
Johnny Knoxville burst onto the showbiz scene
in 2000 as the de facto host of MTV's Jackass,

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:10.770
a strange, hysterically funny reality show
that became a surprise smash hit and launched

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:12.190
Knoxville to stardom.

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:15.110
"Hi I'm Johnny Knoxville, welcome to Jackass!"

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:22.509
He followed it up with three hit Jackass movies
and acting roles in several other films.

00:00:22.509 --> 00:00:25.570
And then Knoxville…pretty much up and vanished.

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:26.570
Why?

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:30.319
Here's a look at the real reasons we don't
hear from Johnny Knoxville anymore.

00:00:30.319 --> 00:00:31.919
He's not much of an actor

00:00:31.919 --> 00:00:35.570
Johnny Knoxville may be a star, but that doesn't
make him an actor.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:40.059
After the success of Jackass on both the small
and big screens, Knoxville landed roles in

00:00:40.059 --> 00:00:43.680
films like The Dukes of Hazzard, Walking Tall,
and A Dirty Shame.

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.510
And the less said about The Ringer, the better.

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:47.190
"Do you need a hug?"

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:52.349
"Jeffy doesn't know what's happening to his
body."

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:54.460
"Ok."

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:57.930
None of them did well at the box office or
with critics.

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:02.719
His only live action acting role in a successful
film came way back in 2002 with Men in Black

00:01:02.719 --> 00:01:06.630
II, where he played the same kind of slightly
dumb mischief-maker that he's played in just

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:08.040
about all of his films.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.860
With that kind of box office record and industry
typecasting, it's no wonder we haven't seen

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.670
much of him at the multiplex recently.

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:15.110
"I think I'm gonna be sick."

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:17.030
"You don't wanna do that."

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:18.590
Wounded warrior

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:22.890
This won't come as much of a surprise, but
Knoxville sustained a number of injuries over

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.610
the years working on Jackass.

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:28.810
On the set of the original TV show, an ankle
sprain forced Knoxville to wear a brace for

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:34.509
most of the first season, while on the first
Jackass movie, he was knocked out cold — twice.

00:01:34.509 --> 00:01:38.390
Knoxville would later top that in Jackass
Number Two, claiming he nearly died when a

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:40.170
rocket blew up on him during a stunt.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:42.970
"3...2...1...go!"

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:49.799
"Hahaha ahahaha!"

00:01:49.799 --> 00:01:54.000
Yet no amount of concussions could compare
to Knoxville's worst injury: he broke his

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:59.329
own penis and tore his urethra when a 400-pound
motorcycle landed on his groin.

00:01:59.329 --> 00:02:02.700
To this day, Knoxville must use a catheter
twice a day.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:07.579
"Why couldn't I have got a broken arm or leg,
or like broken collar - but no!

00:02:07.579 --> 00:02:09.879
I got blood shootin' out of my peepee."

00:02:09.879 --> 00:02:13.980
With so many injuries plaguing him, Knoxville
just isn't able to do as much in general as

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.010
he used to, which may have led to less time
in front of the cameras overall.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:19.849
A Jackass no more

00:02:19.849 --> 00:02:23.459
While the fame brought on by Jackass helped
Knoxville branch out into acting, it also

00:02:23.459 --> 00:02:28.870
posed an immediate problem: how could an ultra-famous
star continue to perform pranks on an unsuspecting

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:29.870
public?

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:33.620
Well, the films addressed this by sending
Knoxville overseas to perform his stunts,

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.910
filming in Japan, Russia, and India.

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:40.740
And that costs a lot of money, time, and resources,
meaning Knoxville may have actually become

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.129
more famous than he can afford to be.

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:46.609
"Hello my name's Johnny Knoxville and I'm
about to end this movie!"

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:51.099
Ryan Dunn's death

00:02:51.099 --> 00:02:55.820
The Jackass franchise took a major hit in
2011 when Knoxville's co-star and close friend

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:59.400
Ryan Dunn died in a car accident at age 34.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.879
Following Dunn's death, Knoxville released
a public statement that read,

00:03:02.879 --> 00:03:07.230
"You'll have to excuse me, I'm just very sad
because I lost my brother and my world got

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:09.420
about 134-percent less funny.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:13.930
I don't know what else to say right now, so
I will close with I love you, Ryan.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:19.050
I have a lot of emotions swirling, but I want
you to know I love you so very much."

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:23.890
Shortly after Dunn's death, Knoxville spun
off from the Jackass brand with the 2013 comedy

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:27.959
Bad Grandpa, which blended hidden-camera pranks
with a scripted story.

00:03:27.959 --> 00:03:32.090
The film proved to be a financial success
and may have shown Knoxville a way forward

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:35.690
despite losing Dunn — and without Jackass.

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:37.319
Smaller projects

00:03:37.319 --> 00:03:41.350
It's not so much that Knoxville has left the
spotlight than the spotlight has left him.

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:44.810
Knoxville has continued to work on smaller
projects that simply haven't gotten as much

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:49.670
attention as Jackass once brought, like the
2013 Arnold Schwarzenegger flop, The Last

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:50.670
Stand.

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:54.670
Following his semi-scripted turn in Bad Grandpa,
Knoxville worked on two independent projects,

00:03:54.670 --> 00:04:00.590
both slated for release in 2016: Weightless,
opposite Julianne Nicholson, and Above Suspicion,

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:02.910
with Game of Thrones star Emilia Clarke.

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:06.850
Working on indie dramas like these could help
Knoxville finally get out of Hollywood typecast

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:07.850
jail.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:10.500
"Oh we gonna have to get out of here."

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:11.840
Not the tabloid type

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:16.269
Finally, this may come as a surprise to some
fans, but Johnny Knoxville has a happy life

00:04:16.269 --> 00:04:17.269
as a family man.

00:04:17.269 --> 00:04:21.350
A father of three, he actually credits impending
fatherhood with helping him jump-start his

00:04:21.350 --> 00:04:22.350
career.

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:26.230
Before the birth of his oldest daughter Madison,
and in need of money to support his forthcoming

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:30.240
family, he brainstormed an idea that would
eventually change his life.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:34.070
"I saw something on TV where a guy pepper
sprayed himself.

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:37.360
And I thought, 'Well that's a really good
idea, that'd be a really good article, if

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:40.940
I could test different types of self-defense
equipment on myself.'

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:46.320
And it was just an article, but Jeff said
'You should, we'll film it for ya too.'"

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:50.600
Those videos proved to be so hilarious that
they are what originally led to the creation

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:51.680
of Jackass.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.680
That's put food on the table, but his quiet
family life and happy marriage to second wife

00:04:55.680 --> 00:05:00.021
Naomi Nelson have kept paparazzi away and
helped Knoxville avoid the harsh glare of

00:05:00.021 --> 00:05:01.620
the tabloid spotlight.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:03.020
He's earned the break.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:04.840
"Hey is this okay?

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:06.200
Then we're good."

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.570
Thanks for watching!

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:10.970
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:14.230
And leave us a comment to let us know what
you want to see from Johnny Knoxville next...

